{"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://atlasly/workspace/v15.html","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://atlasly/workspace/v15.html"}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Nearby Mapped Places"},"description":"Purpose: find mapped nearby schools, shops and services worldwide. When to use: compare local place context around a known site, or prepare mapped points for QGIS. Returns: selected OpenStreetMap point categories from fixed regional sources, straight-line distances in metres, per-layer coverage, source references, an inspectable map and GeoJSON. Limitations: community mapping, not official access evidence or a complete inventory; source freshness, entrances, opening hours and public/wheelchair access are unverified. No walking routes, travel times, parks, bus stops, rail stations or transit frequency; do not infer a walk score or 15-minute-city verdict. Parameter guidance: supply address with country, a prior site_ref, or WGS84 coordinates {lat,lng} with explicit country_code. Non-UK address lookup requires the configured service. Persona selects default category groups; explicit categories can request only mapped schools, hospitals or other supported point types. Radius is 250 to 1000 metres. Missing data means unknown, never absence of services. Chaining: every response returns site_ref; pass it unchanged into another Atlasly tool to reuse the canonical site, coordinates, boundary confidence, LPA, evidence links, and project context.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"address":{"description":"Site address or postcode, with town and country outside the UK. Alternatively pass site_ref from an earlier result; do not send both for different locations.","maxLength":300,"minLength":3,"type":"string"},"categories":{"description":"Optional explicit mapped categories, for example school or hospital. Overrides persona defaults; not complete nearest-place coverage.","items":{"enum":["school","kindergarten","pharmacy","hospital","clinic","cafe","restaurant","bus_station","supermarket","convenience","bakery"],"type":"string"},"maxItems":11,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"coordinates":{"description":"User-supplied WGS84 point {lat, lng}. Send with country_code. The point is not reverse-geocoded, so its address and planning jurisdiction stay unverified.","properties":{"lat":{"maximum":84,"minimum":-80,"type":"number"},"lng":{"maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"}},"required":["lat","lng"],"type":"object"},"country_code":{"description":"ISO two-letter country code such as gb, us, in or fr. Required with coordinates and for addresses outside the UK.","pattern":"^[a-z]{2}$","type":"string"},"persona":{"enum":["general","family","commuter","resident"],"type":"string"},"radius_meters":{"description":"Search radius in metres around the site. Requests above the caller's limit (1,000 m without an account, 2,000 m with one) are reduced or rejected.","maximum":1000,"minimum":250,"type":"integer"},"site_ref":{"description":"Canonical site_ref returned by any previous Atlasly tool. Pass it unchanged to chain the same resolved site into this call; address, search_area, or project_id will be filled from it when omitted.","properties":{"address_aliases":{"items":{"maxLength":300,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"maxItems":4,"type":"array"},"boundary_confidence":{"enum":["address_point","inferred_parcel","red_line_upload","unknown"],"type":"string"},"boundary_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"canonical_address":{"type":["string","null"]},"coordinates":{"anyOf":[{"properties":{"lat":{"type":"number"},"lng":{"type":"number"}},"required":["lat","lng"],"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]},"country_code":{"pattern":"^[a-z]{2}$","type":"string"},"id":{"type":["string","null"]},"jurisdiction":{"type":["string","null"]},"local_planning_authority":{"type":["string","null"]},"location_source":{"enum":["geocoder","user_coordinates"],"type":"string"},"project_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"source_links":{"items":{"properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"url":{"format":"uri","type":"string"}},"required":["label","url"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"status":{"enum":["resolved","partial","unresolved"],"type":"string"},"version":{"const":"1","type":"string"}},"required":["version","status","id","canonical_address","coordinates","boundary_id","boundary_confidence","jurisdiction","local_planning_authority","source_links","project_id"],"type":"object"}},"type":"object"},"name":"get_nearby_mapped_places","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"atlasly_link":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label","url"],"type":"object"},"confidence_notes":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"details":{"additionalProperties":{},"propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"error_code":{"type":"string"},"error_source":{"type":"string"},"executive_summary":{"type":"string"},"headline":{"type":"string"},"human_message":{"type":"string"},"key_data_points":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"confidence":{"enum":["high","medium","low"],"type":"string"},"label":{"type":"string"},"provenance":{"enum":["official_data","policy_citation","atlasly_inference","user_input"],"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label","value","confidence","provenance"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"message":{"type":"string"},"next_best_actions":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"query":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"address":{"type":"string"},"country_code":{"type":"string"},"display_name":{"type":"string"},"geocode_confidence":{"enum":["exact","postcode_only","district_approximation","user_supplied"],"type":"string"},"jurisdiction":{"type":"string"},"lat":{"type":"number"},"lng":{"type":"number"},"local_authority":{"type":"string"},"l